{"id": "EUVD-2026-80888", "enisaUuid": "d0dd014b-9f45-3810-becd-0a47826a106a", "description": "A flaw was found in sequoia-openpgp. The library incorrectly infers key flags for older certificates when a key flags subpacket is missing, leading to a discrepancy in how key capabilities are viewed. This key flag confusion allows an attacker to bypass the back-signature check. Consequently, an attacker can illegitimately bind an arbitrary subkey to their own certificate and forge signatures, completely compromising cryptographic integrity.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T16:56:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T14:40:31", "baseScore": 7.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:34160", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:42078", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:42902", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:76733", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:76734", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:76735", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:76737", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:79357", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-42784", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2464122"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g33h-rrj9-75qv", "CVE-2026-42784"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "176311a0-25b6-3b36-b8fe-1482c39cf98f", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Hardened Images", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0.3.2-4.hum1"}, {"id": "23dc63e8-8414-3780-a418-01d2fed44bc0", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.4.0.1-2.el10_2"}, {"id": "6ecce82c-6aa6-346e-9a28-45337ec231fc", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.10.2.1-1.el9_8"}, {"id": "742dfead-51af-3b7b-b1cf-5876fd4ee921", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise L